  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Cauchy's Integral Formula [S+N]\n\nThe deepest single result of complex analysis. If $f$ is holomorphic on an open set containing a closed disc $\\overline{D_R(z_0)}$, then for any $z$ in the interior\n\n$$f(z) = \\frac{1}{2\\pi i} \\oint_{|\\zeta - z_0| = R} \\frac{f(\\zeta)}{\\zeta - z}\\,d\\zeta.$$\n\nIn words: **values of a holomorphic function inside a disc are determined by its values on the boundary.** That's a wildly more rigid property than smooth real functions have — $C^\\infty$ on $\\mathbb{R}$ has no analogous boundary-value control.\n\nThree consequences land immediately:\n\n1. **Holomorphic ⇒ infinitely differentiable.** Differentiate the integrand under the integral sign.\n2. **Holomorphic ⇒ analytic.** The function equals its Taylor series locally.\n3. **Maximum modulus principle.** $|f|$ on a domain attains its max on the boundary.\n\nThis notebook walks the formula and these consequences.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Verifying the formula numerically [S+N]\n\nTake $f(z) = z^2 + 1$ (entire) and $z_0 = 0$, $R = 1$. The formula at $z = 0.3 + 0.4i$ predicts $f(0.3 + 0.4i) = (0.3 + 0.4i)^2 + 1$.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "f_eval(z) := z^2 + 1$\nz_check : 0.3 + 0.4 * %i$\ntruth_val : expand(f_eval(z_check))$\nprint(\"f(0.3 + 0.4i) =\", truth_val, \"  (=\", float(realpart(truth_val)),\n      \"+\", float(imagpart(truth_val)), \"i)\")$\n\n/* Approximate the contour integral on |ζ| = 1 numerically */\nN_pts : 2000$\ndt : 2 * float(%pi) / N_pts$\ntotal : 0 + 0*%i$\nfor k : 0 thru N_pts - 1 do block([t, zeta, num, den],\n  t : k * dt,\n  zeta : exp(%i * t),\n  num : f_eval(zeta) * %i * exp(%i * t),\n  den : zeta - z_check,\n  total : total + num / den * dt)$\nformula_val : total / (2 * float(%pi) * %i)$\nprint(\"Cauchy formula prediction:\", formula_val)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
