    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Cauchy's formula for derivatives\n\nDifferentiate under the integral sign:\n\n$$f^{(n)}(z) = \\frac{n!}{2\\pi i} \\oint \\frac{f(\\zeta)}{(\\zeta - z)^{n+1}}\\,d\\zeta.$$\n\nIn particular, **all derivatives exist** as soon as one does. For $f(z) = z^2 + 1$ at $z = 0$, $f''(0) = 2$. Verify:\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* Numerical: f''(0) = 2! / (2πi) ∮ f(ζ)/ζ³ dζ */\ntotal2 : 0 + 0*%i$\nfor k : 0 thru N_pts - 1 do block([t, zeta, num, den],\n  t : k * dt,\n  zeta : exp(%i * t),\n  num : f_eval(zeta) * %i * exp(%i * t),\n  den : zeta^3,\n  total2 : total2 + num / den * dt)$\nfpp_val : 2.0 * total2 / (2 * float(%pi) * %i)$\nprint(\"f''(0) via Cauchy formula:\", fpp_val)$\nprint(\"(true f''(0) = 2)\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 7,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
